# Lilv 0.28.0's world_load_plugin_classes leaves one 24-byte class allocation
# unreachable when the process-lifetime LV2 catalog is loaded. Suppress only
# this known third-party allocation; other SkyAPO/LV2 allocations remain checked.
leak:lilv_world_load_plugin_classes
# Qt 6 / FreeType retain process-global font caches until QApplication teardown
# in the offscreen editor test. The suppressed stack root is in Qt cleanup, not
# a LinuxAPO-owned allocation.
leak:QGuiApplicationPrivate::cleanupThreadData
# Qt's offscreen response-plot paint path also populates Fontconfig's global
# fallback-font cache. Those allocations remain rooted in Fontconfig/FreeType
# after QApplication teardown; suppress only their font lookup/initialization
# entry points, not general Qt or application allocations.
leak:FcFontMatch
leak:FT_Init_FreeType
